  (text "NOTES      設計說明" (at 184.15 97.79 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 60d3ede7-456b-48aa-87f3-d24b1ad9d1aa)
  )
  (text "1. RJ9 (4P4C) pinout is NOT standardized. Measure first:\n   - receiver pair: 30~300 ohm DC; electret mic pair: diode-like (asymmetric).\n   - swap J2 pin assignment to match your handset.\n2. Path A: LM386 has low output impedance, so the receiver no longer\n   loads the PC line out -> no volume drop. RV1 sets the level.\n   Gain fixed at 20 (pins 1/8 open). C5 blocks the 2.5 V DC offset.\n   R3 limits current into the receiver (telephone receiver ~1 mW rated).\n3. Path B: electret needs 2~5 V bias via R5. Mic level ~10 mV -> line\n   level ~300 mV needs ~30 dB; set with RV2. Output impedance ~100 ohm\n   drives the 10 kohm line in without loss.\n   Dynamic mic instead of electret: remove R5, raise gain (2 stages).\n4. Ground: everything is powered from the same PC USB port -> single\n   ground reference. Star ground on PCB; keep U2 away from U1 output.\n   R6/C7 filter USB switching noise for the mic preamp (+5V_FILT).\n5. Optional sidetone: 47k~100k from U2A output to RV1 pin 1.\n6. Optional LDO (e.g. 4.5 V) in place of R6 if USB noise is still audible.\n7. SMT: R/C 0805; 10uF/22uF = 1206 X5R 10V ceramic; 47pF = C0G;\n   U1/U2 = SOIC-8; RV2 = Bourns 3314J SMT trimmer; FB1 = 0805 bead.\n   THT (connectors + panel pot): J1/J3 = CUI SJ1-3523N 3.5 mm jack,\n   J2 = Evercom 5301-440 RJ9, J4 = Lumberg 2411 02 USB-B,\n   RV1 = Alps RK097 single 9 mm right-angle shaft pot.\n8. C5/C7/C14 = SMD V-chip electrolytic 6.3 mm, >= 6.3 V rating." (at 185.42 101.6 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left top))
    (uuid a36f0b10-d343-4de3-933f-c1f17c092650)
  )
